# ===================================================================
# Project wrap-up (2026-06): tracked exceptions + local-only artifacts
# (placed last so these rules override the broad patterns above)
# ===================================================================

# Empirical routing leaderboard: runtime DATA the recommender reads at import.
# The broad `data` rule above would drop it, silently disabling empirical
# re-ranking on a fresh clone. Keep it tracked.
!agent/spatialomicsgym/data/
!agent/spatialomicsgym/data/empirical_leaderboard.json

# Manuscript deliverable: version-control the small (~12MB) headline artifacts
# (tables, figures, summaries, aggregation/figure code, reproducibility runbook).
# The `manuscript/` rule above ignores the whole tree; re-include it but keep OUT
# the absolute-path symlink trees (they point into the 669GB results + external
# 101GB) — raw per-cell results stay ignored and live on disk only.
!agent/benchmarks/manuscript/
agent/benchmarks/manuscript/per_cell_results/
agent/benchmarks/manuscript/tool_outputs/
agent/benchmarks/manuscript/code/evaluation/
agent/benchmarks/manuscript/code/manual_runners/

# The SpatialBench paper itself (2.7 MB of third-party PDF) sits at agent/benchmarks/SpatialBench.pdf so
# the Fig-7 scripts beside it can be read against their source. It is not our artifact and not
# source: the rule above version-controls the ~12 MB of *our* headline deliverables, and a
# redistributable copy of someone else's paper is neither of those things. Kept on disk, cited in
# agent/benchmarks/manuscript/figures/fig7_caption.md.
agent/benchmarks/SpatialBench.pdf

# Large local-only artifacts — kept on disk, catalogued in docs/REPO_MAP.md and
# demo_outputs/MANIFEST.md, never committed (too big / not source).
demo_outputs/
demo_datasets_for_3D_analysis/
# The curated 63-sample spatial library (27 GB of .h5ad), moved into the checkout from
# /workspace/spatial_library_backup on 2026-10-06. Its catalog is tracked in
# agent/spatialomicsgym/data/spatial_library/registry.json; the data never is.
/spatial_library/
# The deployment's tool-output root (SOG_WORK_DIR in .env), in the checkout since 2026-10-06 instead
# of /workspace/work. Run output, never source.
/work/
# _safety/ is a local run-log scratch tree (2.2 GB here, nothing that belongs in the repo). It used
# to be listed one file pattern at a time, which covered the logs that existed and nothing else: a
# notes.json, results.txt, scratch.py or plot.png written there was untracked, unignored, and
# offered to the next `git add -A`. Ignoring the directory covers the shapes nobody predicted; the
# specific rules below are kept because they document what lives in there. Two files (_PINNED_STATUS.md
# and test_mcp_tool_routing.py) had been committed out of this tree and were removed with the rest of
# the scratch cleanup -- so this rule now contradicts nothing, which
# test_repo_hygiene.py::test_no_tracked_file_is_ignored enforces.
_safety/
_safety/_logs/
_safety/_brain_demo_logs/
_safety/live_a1_default_tool_results*/
_safety/mcp_3d_tool_tests_*/
_safety/_live_smoke_*.log

# Archived scratch/backups (kept locally, not committed)
_archive/

# Scratch test outputs + stray artifacts (kept locally, not committed)
agent/benchmarks/system_tests/
agent/benchmarks/creation_deletion/
agent/tools/*.pt
# Machine-local timestamped snapshots of the generated setup config (superseded
# copies kept beside the live file); never committed.
install/recipes/mcp_config.setup.yaml.stale-*

# Pre-edit backups left beside the file they are a copy of -- `cluster_comparison.py.pre_v8`,
# `...pre_v12`. Four exist in this tree right now, and each is a byte-copy of a file that IS
# tracked, so a `git add -A` ships the same source twice under a name nothing imports, nothing
# tests and no reader can date. Checked before the rule was written: NOTHING matching it is
# tracked. That order matters -- a pattern that shadows an already-tracked path does not untrack
# anything, it only tells the next reader a lie about what git is doing.
*.pre_v[0-9]*

# `node_modules/` at ANY depth.
node_modules/
_safety/live_a1_default_tool_test.py
_safety/run_live_a1_default_tool_test.sh

# User-created tool runtime artifacts (generated by the creation system; regenerated on reproduce)
agent/tools_user/*_worker.py
agent/tools_user/*_worker.R
agent/tools_user/*_mcp_server.py
agent/tools_user/vendor_*/

# agent/benchmarks/data is CODE (data_registry imported by benchmarks/__init__), not data —
# the broad `data` rule drops it, breaking a fresh clone. Keep it tracked.
!agent/benchmarks/data/
!agent/benchmarks/data/*.py
!agent/benchmarks/data/*.md

# In-repo dataset-library catalog (broad `data` rule would drop it). Keep it tracked so
# search_spatial_datasets + the instance-table generators work without the external library.
!agent/spatialomicsgym/data/
!agent/spatialomicsgym/data/spatial_library/
!agent/spatialomicsgym/data/spatial_library/registry.json

# sog-setup wizard: per-run test results + generated wiring are throwaway (regenerated
# each run). Durable state lives in .sog_setup/ (its own rule near the top of this file).
# install/recipes/tool_specs/ is intentionally NOT ignored — those committed recipes are the
# fresh-clone build inputs. test/installation/ is also inside the wholly ignored /test/ below;
# the line stays so the wizard's artifact dir is covered on its own terms.
test/installation/
install/recipes/mcp_config.setup.yaml
install/recipes/env_overrides.env
# The generic `env/` rule near the top of this file also swallows the wizard's
# committed export recipes; force the directory (and its files) back in — they
# are the fresh-clone build inputs and MUST be tracked.
!install/recipes/tool_specs/env/
!install/recipes/tool_specs/env/*.env.yaml
_live_out/

# huggingface_data/: the builders, the docs and the stats ARE source and are tracked. What they
# emit is a build artifact whose home is the Hub, not git history -- the JSONL corpus, and the
# `hub_repo/` the packager reshapes it into (parquet shards and a generated card). The global
# `*.jsonl` rule covers only the first of those; this rule is about the directory, so no future
# output format silently becomes committable either.
huggingface_data/data/
# Same reasoning for the paper release, this folder's default product: the filter script, the
# runbook and both stats twins are tracked; the filtered slice (JSONL + selection sidecar) and
# the packed upload folder `hub_repo/` are artifacts.
huggingface_data/filtered/
huggingface_data/hub_repo/
# huggingface_data_instance/: the instance release (63-sample library + 4,614 task instances). Its
# scripts, README and stats twin are source; `hub_repo/` is the ~27 GB upload folder (library copies,
# parquet, card) and belongs on the Hub only. Most of its payload (png, json, csv, tif) matches no
# global rule, so without this line one `git add` would pull gigabytes into the index.
huggingface_data_instance/hub_repo/


# 2026-10-07 slimming: the repository carries what the project needs to RUN. The test suite lives in
# test/ on disk (bash agent/spatialomicsgym/spatialomicsgym_env/run_core_tests.sh runs it here) and is
# not tracked at all -- no exceptions: running code that wants the smoke harness or the core-module
# list loads them from test/ by file path and says so when test/ is absent. Per-developer tool state
# is never tracked either.
/test/
/.worktrees/
